## 2. Knowledge Extraction

### Scheme JSON Schema
```json
{
  "scheme_id": "PM-KISAN-001",
  "name": "PM-KISAN Samman Nidhi",
  "name_hindi": "पीएम-किसान सम्मान निधि",
  "department": "Ministry of Agriculture",
  "ministry": "Agriculture & Farmers Welfare",
  "state": "Central",
  "category": ["agriculture", "direct_benefit"],
  "target_beneficiaries": ["farmers", "small_farmers"],
  "eligibility": {
    "age": {"min": 18, "max": null},
    "income": {"max": null},
    "land_ownership": {"required": true, "max_hectares": 2},
    "occupation": ["farmer"],
    "states": ["all"],
    "exclusions": ["institutional_landholders", "income_tax_payers"]
  },
  "benefits": {
    "type": "cash_transfer",
    "amount": 6000,
    "frequency": "annual",
    "installments": 3,
    "description": "₹6,000 per year in three installments"
  },
  "documents_required": ["aadhaar", "land_records", "bank_account"],
  "application_process": ["online_portal", "csc_center"],
  "official_url": "https://pmkisan.gov.in",
  "deadline": null,
  "status": "active",
  "last_updated": "2025-01-15",
  "source_urls": ["https://..."],
  "content_hash": "abc123"
}
```

### Extraction Architecture
```
Raw HTML/PDF → LLM Structured Extraction (Gemini) → Pydantic Validation → Manual Review Queue → Store
```
- Use Gemini with structured output (JSON mode) for extraction
- Pydantic models enforce schema validation
- Confidence scoring: if extraction confidence < 0.8, route to human review
- **Why LLM over NER?** Government scheme pages have inconsistent formats; LLM handles variability better than rule-based NER

